; BRIDGE: descent × homological_algebra [SELF-DIRECTED, 2026-08-02]; Both H^1(G_k, Aut(X)) and Ext^1(M,N) classify objects by their obstruction to triviality. H^1: forms of X are locally trivial (trivialize over k^sep) but globally twisted; cocycle measures descent obstruction. Ext^1: extensions 0→N→E→M→0 are locally split but globally non-split; extension class measures splitting obstruction. When Aut(X) is abelian, nonabelian H^1 reduces to Ext^1 over ZG. G-torsor = principal homogeneous space = extension of trivial object by G. Categorical unity: both are first cohomology, abelian or nonabelian.(|- ((==> (&& (--> Field $k) (--> GaloisGroup $G $k) (--> Object $X) (--> Forms $X $k) (--> LocallyTrivial (Forms $X $k) (SeparableClosure $k)) (--> Obstruction (H1 $G (Aut $X))))) (--> DescentObstruction $k $X)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Module $M $R) (--> Module $N $R) (--> Extensions $E $M $N) (--> LocallySplit $E) (--> Obstruction (Ext1 $M $N)))) (--> ExtensionObstruction $R $M $N)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ObstructionByCohomology $O1) (--> ObstructionByCohomology $O2) (--> Equals (Type $O1) FirstCohomology) (--> Equals (Type $O2) FirstCohomology) (--> Generalizes (NonabelianH1 $G $A) (Ext1 $M $N)) (--> ReducesTo (NonabelianH1 $G $A) (Ext1 $M $N) (AbelianGroup $A)))) (--> StructuralBridge $O1 $O2)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
